from tnx import *
def T(iy,iyn,*a): TA(9,iy,iyn,*a)
I1="Iyal 1: Language (மொழி)"
T(1,I1,"tamil-vidu-thoothu","Tamil Vidu Thoothu (தமிழ்விடு தூது)",
 "What if a poet used the Tamil language itself as the messenger?",
 "Tamil Vidu Thoothu is a poem of the thoothu type, a short literary form (சிற்றிலக்கியம்) in which a messenger such as a parrot, swan or cloud carries a message. Here the poet makes Tamil itself the messenger, praising its sweetness, literary wealth, poetic variety, taste and beauty. Its opening lines call Tamil a sweet nectar and the fruit of liberation, and speak of the three Tamils: iyal, isai and nadakam (முத்தமிழ்).",
 "The poem shows how a poet can express pride in the mother tongue. It presents Tamil as a language that can express every poetic form and every feeling, so people should love and protect it.",
 "Notice the words தூது (a message), சிற்றிலக்கியம் (a minor genre of literature), முத்தமிழ் (three Tamils), பா வகைகள் (verse forms) and தேன் (honey, a metaphor for sweetness). This is a memorisation poem (மனப்பாடப் பகுதி) in the textbook.",
 ["தூது","சிற்றிலக்கியம்","முத்தமிழ்","தெள்ளமுது","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("The messenger in this poem is a parrot.",["The messenger is Tamil itself.","The poem praises Tamil."]),
 ["m|In Tamil Vidu Thoothu, who is the messenger?|The Tamil language|A parrot|A swan|Tamil is the thoothu.","m|Muthamizh means|iyal, isai and nadakam|three kings|three seas|The three branches of Tamil.","t|Thoothu is a minor literary genre.|T|It is a சிற்றிலக்கியம்.","m|The poem compares Tamil to|sweet nectar|a stone|iron|It praises sweetness.","s|What is the Tamil word for a message-carrying poem?|thoothu;தூது|It is a thoothu.","t|The poem insults Tamil.|F|It praises Tamil."])
T(1,I1,"dravida-mozhikkudumbam","The Dravidian Language Family (திராவிட மொழிக்குடும்பம்)",
 "Tamil has many sister languages, and linguists group them into one family.",
 "This prose piece explains that Tamil is the senior language among the Dravidian languages and can meet the demands of every age and every kind of newness. Scholars of other countries who studied Tamil have praised its classical excellence (செம்மொழி). The lesson compares Tamil with other languages of the family.",
 "It describes how, in early times, people shared thoughts through gestures, sounds and drawings, and slowly developed languages. The lesson helps us see where Tamil belongs among the world's languages.",
 "Key terms: திராவிட மொழிக்குடும்பம் (Dravidian family), செம்மொழி (classical language), மொழி (language) and தொன்மை (antiquity). Learn the names of Dravidian languages such as Tamil, Telugu, Kannada and Malayalam.",
 ["மொழிக்குடும்பம்","செம்மொழி","தொன்மை","திராவிடம்","மொழி"],
 ("Tamil is not related to any other language.",["It belongs to the Dravidian family.","It is the senior member."]),
 ["m|Tamil belongs to the|Dravidian family|Indo-European family|Chinese family|The Dravidian language family.","m|செம்மொழி means|classical language|a dialect|a script|Classical language.","t|Early people used gestures before words.|T|Yes.","m|Which is also a Dravidian language?|Telugu|English|French|It is Dravidian.","s|What does தொன்மை mean?|antiquity;ancient|Great age.","t|Tamil can adapt to new times.|T|Yes."])
T(1,I1,"aaraam-thinai","Aaraam Thinai (ஆறாம் திணை, supplementary)",
 "What happens to people who must leave their homeland?",
 "Aaraam Thinai is a supplementary prose piece by A. Muthulingam. It describes the pain of people who are uprooted from their native land, like plants pulled out of the soil, and who must face hardships as refugees or migrants. It records this wound that never heals.",
 "The title means the sixth landscape: the Sangam tradition has five landscapes (ஐந்திணை), and the writer suggests that the world of the displaced is a sixth, painful one. The lesson makes us feel sympathy for refugees and for Tamil people who live abroad.",
 "Terms to know: திணை (landscape category), புலம்பெயர்தல் (migration), தாய்மண் (motherland) and அவலம் (suffering). A supplementary lesson is for reading and understanding rather than for memorising.",
 ["திணை","புலம்பெயர்தல்","தாய்மண்","அவலம்","துணைப்பாடம்"],
 ("Aaraam Thinai is a poem about farming.",["It is about displaced people.","It speaks of homeland and migration."]),
 ["m|Aaraam Thinai is by|A. Muthulingam|Kannadasan|Bharathidasan|A. Muthulingam.","m|It is mainly about|people uprooted from their homeland|a festival|a river|The pain of displacement.","t|The ஆறாம் திணை means the sixth landscape.|T|Yes.","m|புலம்பெயர்தல் means|migration|farming|festival|Moving away from one's land.","s|How many traditional Tamil landscapes (thinai) are there?|five;5|Five.","t|It makes us feel sympathy for the displaced.|T|Yes."])
T(1,I1,"ezhuthu-alapedai","Grammar: Elongation of sound (எழுத்து - அளபெடை)",
 "Sometimes a poet stretches a sound to fit the music of a line.",
 "அளபெடை means the lengthening of a letter's sound beyond its usual duration (மாத்திரை) for the sake of rhythm in a verse. There are two kinds: உயிரளபெடை, the lengthening of a vowel, and ஒற்றளபெடை, the lengthening of a consonant (mei).",
 "In உயிரளபெடை the long vowel is followed by a short vowel of the same kind, written in the line; it is of three types according to its purpose: இசை நிறைத்தல் (செய்யுளிசை), இன்னிசை and சொல்லிசை. These give the line its musical flow.",
 "Practise spotting alapedai in verses, for example the extra vowel written after a long vowel in Thirukkural. Learn the terms எழுத்து, மாத்திரை, உயிர், ஒற்று and செய்யுள்.",
 ["அளபெடை","உயிரளபெடை","ஒற்றளபெடை","மாத்திரை","செய்யுள்"],
 ("Alapedai shortens a sound.",["It lengthens a sound.","It fits the rhythm."]),
 ["m|Alapedai means|lengthening of sound|shortening of sound|silence|The sound is extended.","m|Alapedai occurs mainly in|verse (seyyul)|prose|numbers|For rhythm.","t|Uyir alapedai lengthens a vowel.|T|Yes.","m|Otru alapedai lengthens a|consonant|vowel|word|Mei letter.","s|Name one type of uyir alapedai.|isai niraiththal;innisai;sollisai;இன்னிசை;சொல்லிசை;செய்யுளிசை|There are three types.","t|Alapedai is used for music in poetry.|T|Yes."])
I2="Iyal 2: Nature and Environment (இயற்கை, சுற்றுச்சூழல்)"
T(2,I2,"neerindri-amaiyathu-ulagu","Neerindri Amaiyathu Ulagu (நீரின்றி அமையாது உலகு)",
 "Without water, the world cannot go on, as even an ancient saying warns.",
 "This prose lesson on water begins by calling nature the greatest gift to living things: tall mountains, forests, green meadows, water bodies, fields and groves. It says it is our duty to use these wisely and protect them for the next generation, and so it speaks of water management (நீர் மேலாண்மை).",
 "The lesson shows that ancient Tamils built tanks, canals and dams and valued water. Today water is scarce, so conserving and managing it is a public duty.",
 "Terms: நீர் மேலாண்மை (water management), நீர்நிலை (water body), இயற்கை (nature) and பாதுகாப்பு (protection). The title echoes a line of Thirukkural, which says that the world cannot exist without water.",
 ["நீர்மேலாண்மை","நீர்நிலை","இயற்கை","பாதுகாப்பு","திருக்குறள்"],
 ("Water is not important for the world.",["The world cannot exist without water.","We must manage it."]),
 ["m|The lesson stresses|water management|cooking|dance|Neer melanmai.","m|Who must protect nature for future generations?|All of us|Only kings|Only farmers|It is our duty.","t|The title says the world cannot exist without water.|T|Yes.","m|நீர்நிலை means|water body|fire|house|Tank, lake or river.","s|What does இயற்கை mean?|nature|Nature.","t|Ancient Tamils valued water.|T|Yes."])
T(2,I2,"periyapuranam","Periyapuranam (பெரியபுராணம்) by Sekkizhar",
 "When the canals are strong, water rises, then paddy rises, then the people prosper.",
 "Periyapuranam, composed by Sekkizhar, is the twelfth Thirumurai and tells the lives of the sixty-three Nayanmars. The textbook poem describes the Chola country as a land of water, where the river Kaveri spreads flowers and fertility along its path.",
 "It conveys the saying that when the bunds rise the water rises, when the water rises the paddy rises, and when the paddy rises the people rise. This is the chain of prosperity in a farming country.",
 "Learn the terms புராணம் (epic-like sacred story), நாயன்மார் (Shaiva saints), திருமுறை (sacred Shaiva collection), காவிரி (river Kaveri) and சோழநாடு (Chola country). It is a memorisation poem.",
 ["புராணம்","சேக்கிழார்","காவிரி","சோழநாடு","திருமுறை"],
 ("Periyapuranam is about the Pandya kings.",["It tells of Shaiva saints.","It also praises the Chola country."]),
 ["m|Periyapuranam was composed by|Sekkizhar|Valluvar|Kamban|Sekkizhar.","m|The river praised is|Kaveri|Vaigai|Ganga|The Kaveri.","t|It tells the lives of sixty-three Nayanmars.|T|Yes.","m|Which country is described as a land of water?|Chola country|Chera country|Sri Lanka|Chozha nadu.","s|What does the water raise, according to the saying?|paddy;nel|Water raises paddy.","t|It is a memorisation poem.|T|Yes."])
T(2,I2,"purananuru","Purananuru (புறநானூறு) — a Sangam poem",
 "Sangam poets praised rulers who protected their people and the land.",
 "Purananuru is a Sangam anthology of 400 poems on the outer life (புறம்): war, charity, governance and the ways of the world. The poem in the textbook is a memorisation poem that shows the greatness of the Tamil tradition in the Sangam period.",
 "Purananuru speaks of virtues such as generosity, courage and justice, and it is valued for its picture of ancient Tamil society. Poems such as these inspire us to be kind and just.",
 "Terms: புறநானூறு, புறப்பொருள் (outer themes), எட்டுத்தொகை (eight anthologies) and சங்க இலக்கியம். It has four hundred poems.",
 ["புறநானூறு","புறப்பொருள்","எட்டுத்தொகை","சங்க இலக்கியம்","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("Purananuru has only love poems.",["It speaks of outer life.","It includes war and charity."]),
 ["m|Purananuru belongs to|Ettuthokai|Pathinenkilkanakku|Ainkurunooru|One of the eight anthologies.","m|Purananuru has how many poems?|400|100|1330|It has 400 poems.","t|It describes outer life such as war and charity.|T|Yes.","m|It belongs to which period?|Sangam|Modern|Colonial|The Sangam age.","s|What is புறம் in English?|outer life;outer|Outer themes.","t|It is a Sangam text.|T|Yes."])
T(2,I2,"thanneer","Thanneer (தண்ணீர்) — short story by Kandharvan",
 "In a village where water is scarce, even a small act of kindness can matter.",
 "Thanneer is a short story by Kandharvan about the water crisis in small villages, which has become a serious problem of daily life. Literature has stressed the need of water since ancient times, and the story brings out how the shortage affects ordinary people.",
 "The story begins with a harsh sun and makes us feel the thirst of the village. It teaches that water is precious, that we should share it and care for sources.",
 "Notice how a short story (சிறுகதை) builds a mood through description of the weather and place. Learn the words தண்ணீர், வறட்சி (drought), சிற்றூர் (small village) and நெருக்கடி (crisis).",
 ["சிறுகதை","தண்ணீர்","வறட்சி","சிற்றூர்","நெருக்கடி"],
 ("Thanneer is a poem.",["It is a short story.","It is by Kandharvan."]),
 ["m|Thanneer is a|short story|epic|drama|Siru kathai.","m|The story is by|Kandharvan|Sekkizhar|Bharathidasan|Kandharvan.","t|It is about water scarcity.|T|Yes.","m|வறட்சி means|drought|flood|festival|Dry period.","s|What does சிறுகதை mean in English?|short story|Short story.","t|The crisis is felt strongly in small villages.|T|Yes."])
T(2,I2,"pagupatha-uruppilakkanam","Grammar: Parts of a word (பகுபத உறுப்பிலக்கணம்)",
 "A Tamil word can be split into parts, like a machine into its pieces.",
 "A பகுபதம் is a word that can be broken into meaningful parts. The six parts (உறுப்புகள்) are பகுதி (root), விகுதி (ending), இடைநிலை (middle suffix), சாரியை (a linking syllable), சந்தி (joining sound) and விகாரம் (change).",
 "To analyse a word, split it into these parts. For example, கொள்வார் can be written as கொள் + வ் + ஆர், where கொள் is the root, வ் is a future tense marker and ஆர் is a plural honorific ending.",
 "Practise dividing verbs and nouns and naming each part. Remember that every பகுபதம் must have at least a பகுதி and a விகுதி.",
 ["பகுபதம்","பகுதி","விகுதி","இடைநிலை","சாரியை"],
 ("A word has no parts.",["A பகுபதம் has parts.","Root and ending are essential."]),
 ["m|பகுதி means|the root|the ending|the tense|The base of a word.","m|விகுதி is the|ending|root|middle|Ending part.","t|A பகுபதம் can be split.|T|Yes.","m|How many உறுப்புகள் are there?|Six|Two|Ten|Six.","s|What is the middle letter or syllable called?|இடைநிலை;idainilai|The middle suffix.","t|இடைநிலை shows tense.|T|In verbs, yes."])
